course: dictionary
lesson: 501
title: Aspen and the trembling leaf
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An aspen is a tall, thin tree whose round leaves sit on long, flat stalks, so even the slightest wind makes them shake and flutter. «Trembling like an aspen leaf» means shaking, often with fear.
explain: Context gives you clues. «A grove of aspens can grow from one shared root system.» A grove is a small group of trees growing close together, and here the trees are joined under the ground by one root system.
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If «grove» means a small group of trees, does «a small group of trees can grow from one shared root system» make sense? It does, so you have found the meaning.
fact: An aspen is a tall, thin tree of the poplar family.
fact: Its round leaves grow on long, flat stalks, so they shake in the slightest wind.
fact: «Quaking aspen» and «trembling aspen» both describe these fluttering leaves.
fact: «Pando in Utah is a group of aspen trees that are all one plant joined by the same roots.»
fact: Aspen wood is light and soft.
exercise: «A grove of aspens can grow from one shared root system.» What does grove mean here? | A deep, dark cave under the ground | A cold, fast river | *A small group of trees growing together | A tall stone castle
exercise: She stood trembling like an aspen leaf before the test. What feeling does this suggest? | Joy at a birthday party | Hunger after lunch | *Fear | Cold from swimming
exercise: Why do aspen leaves shake so easily? | They are glued firmly to the branch | They are made of metal | They are heavy fruit | *Their long, flat stalks let them flutter in the slightest wind
test:
Aspen wood is what kind of wood? | Heavy and hard | *Light and soft | Wet and cold | Shiny and metal
In autumn, aspen leaves turn which colour? | Bright blue | Pure white | *Bright gold | Deep black
exam:
Pando is a huge aspen grove in which American state? | Florida | *Utah | Colorado | Alaska
